  <page_number>54</page_number>
  <running_head>I. IACOMOTI</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <p>Tentauit, eheu! sub duce Barbaro</p>
    <l>Gallus? Tyrannorumque signa</l>
    <l>Hospita Guisiadum sequutus</l>
    <l>Funesta Gallis praelia cinibus</l>
    <l>Impune mouit? Ruraque feruido</l>
    <l>Sulcata Francorum labore</l>
    <l>Marte suo populata vidit?</l>
    <l>Quum sceptra Genti Gallica perfida,</l>
    <l>Et fraudulento prodidit hospiti:</l>
    <l>Quum iussa vellet subiugatos</l>
    <l>Francigenas Lotharinga ferre?</l>
    <l>Tali superbis milite, Guisie,</l>
    <l>Regnumque poscis, quidlibet impotens</l>
    <l>Sperare, per vastas ruentis</l>
    <l>Dum patriae furit ille cades.</l>
    <l>Sic regna Stirpi debita regiae</l>
    <l>Galloque captas aduena principi?</l>
    <l>Sic prisca Legum sacra turbas</l>
    <l>Et Salicae pia iura Normae?</l>
    <l>Te blandienti somnus imagine,</l>
    <l>Te mentis error ludit amabilis:</l>
    <l>Quum sceptra Gallorum lacertis</l>
    <l>Grandia non paribus prehensas.</l>
    <l>Qui regna terris diuidit omnibus,</l>
    <l>Qui regna firmat legibus additis</l>
    <l>Tremendus author, Gentibusque</l>
    <l>Iura dedit, violanda nulli:</l>
    <l>Qui cuncta rubri fulminis ignibus</l>
    <l>Terret</l>
  </main_text>
  <notes>Verse text; the words "Terret" at lower right may be a catchword. Long s rendered as s; the "Stirpi", "Galloque" lines and the words "Guisiadum", "Guisie" are as printed. Some words in the right margin are faint show-through and are omitted.</notes>
